#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Applies the prediction-double feature (per-fixture kickoff lock, double
multiplier, `missed` grade) across domain / application / infrastructure /
contracts / the HTTP edge / composition root, plus the new migration.

Run from the repo root (/workspaces/nukhbaa):
    python3 apply_prediction_double.py

Each touched file is patched via a sequence of exact str.replace hunks.
Before touching a file, it is compared to its fully-patched target content —
if it already matches, the file is skipped untouched (safe to re-run).
Otherwise each hunk's search text must appear EXACTLY ONCE in the file right
before it is applied; if it's missing or ambiguous (file changed since this
script was generated, partially hand-edited, etc.) the script stops
immediately with an explicit error naming the file and hunk index, and
nothing is written. The new migration file is created only if it does not
already exist.
"""
